{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "art_direction": "Episode 01 immersive scene compositor: stable production background asset slot + authored multi-plane field props + production character WebP layers + node-specific mood/focus.",
  "rules": [
    "Every authored Episode 01 event has a visual scene.",
    "Dialogue nodes spotlight the actual speaker.",
    "Choice nodes visually tighten framing before the decision.",
    "Result nodes change grade/focus from the selected result node instead of showing a generic static background.",
    "Visuals never label a choice correct or incorrect.",
    "Each environment resolves through a stable production background asset id; final WebP replaces RC without event/content changes.",
    "Priority construction beats use at least two independently positioned foreground/midground field elements so the scene reads as a place, not a flat backdrop.",
    "Inspection conflict beats keep hazard evidence and control measures visible at the same time so field pressure and safety control remain legible together.",
    "Responsibility/report beats add a neutral evidence-board layer for records and timeline context; the board never marks a side as correct."
  ],
